###################
*.com
*.class
*.dll
*.exe
*.o
*.so

# Ignore Python Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files #
#######################################################
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.bak
*.npz

# data files for MakeHuman  Project #
#####################################
*.obj
*.png
*.thumb
*.mhclo
*.mhmat
*.mhpose
*.meta
*.mhuv
*.mhw
*.proxy
*.mhpxy
*.list
*.bvh
*.mhskel
# (data/ moved to the repo root in the 2026-08-29 restructure and is tracked)
#
# Those asset-extension rules predate the move and would now silently drop
# anything new under data/ -- the generated mixamo_superset.mhskel was ignored
# on creation, which would have failed the CI staleness gate on its first run
# because the file was never committed. The tracked assets only survive because
# they were added before the rules. Everything under data/ is repo content.
!data/**
# Same reason for resources/: it is curated repo content -- icons, fonts,
# shaders and the branding assets -- and the blanket `*.png` above would
# otherwise silently drop the app icon, leaving a clone with no Dock icon and
# no error to explain it.
!resources/**
# And for tests/: every fixture there is repo content -- parity data captured
# from the Python oracle, and small hand-written files a refusal test needs.
# `*.mhpose` above silently dropped `tests/golden/mhpose/smirk.mhpose` on its
# first commit -- `git add -A` says nothing about an ignored file -- so the .bin
# and cases.json went in, the file the loader parses did not, and CI failed on a
# fresh checkout while the local run passed.
#
# Scoped to `tests/**` rather than `tests/golden/**` because the narrower rule
# immediately caught the next one out: `tests/expression_bad_unit.mhpose`, a
# refusal fixture one directory up, was ignored again the very next chunk.
!tests/**
base_1-1_contents.txt

